abstract: >-
  Evolution by Emergence is an open research corpus and machine-auditable
  candidate architecture for resource-constrained cumulative evolution.
  Version v22.2 makes persistence the premise of the formal core. From
  substrate dependence with a finite buffer and reciprocal support, it derives
  that persistence requires correctability: the correctability aim of earlier
  versions becomes a theorem, and a countermodel shows reciprocity is
  load-bearing. From an open-ended world and positive upkeep, it derives that
  persistence requires the vortex to keep turning, without claiming that it
  does. CORE.md is reframed as one premise, two consequences and five laws;
  formalization/ebe-core/EbECore.lean now audits 44 machine-checked results;
  and PREDICTIONS.md states falsifiable predictions about collectives of
  fallible intelligences, with SCAP as a conditional design result. The
  release title uses "simulation of reality" to mean the internal model
  through which a system experiences and acts in the world, not a claim that
  reality itself is simulated. Formal verification establishes implications
  under explicit premises; empirical, causal, political and normative
  interpretations remain open.
keywords:
